# .graphifyignore — what to exclude from the knowledge graph (see ../PROTOCOL.md §9).
# Same syntax as .gitignore, including ! negation.
#
# Graphify runs with THIS directory as its root (`/graphify knowledge_base --update`), so every
# path in the graph is knowledge-base-relative — `peskas/kenya_validated_trips.csv`, never
# `knowledge_base/peskas/...`. That is required: the first path segment is an initiative name
# throughout the system (see ../wdb_paths.py).
#
# The long list of application excludes this file used to carry (mode_a/, mode_b/, wdb_router/,
# read-ui/, tests/, docs/, proof*/, model_eval/, cost_sim/, …) is gone — those live in the app
# repo root, outside graphify's root, so they can no longer leak into the corpus at all.

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
*.generated.*

# NOTE: graphify-out/ is deliberately NOT excluded — graphify converts binaries (.docx/.pdf) into
# graphify-out/converted/ and reads that text back as the extraction proxy. Excluding it would
# silently drop those documents from the graph. Graphify manages the directory itself.

# Per-initiative helper scripts that ship next to the data they converted.
convert_pondcube.py
